n the Babylonian Talmud: introduction and studies / edited by Tal Ilan [and others]."10g[I].tIntroduction and studies /redited by Tal Ilan, Tamara Or, Dorothea M. Salzer, Christiane Steuer, Irina Wandrey ; 2007 --gI/2. Tractates Pe'ah, Demai and Kil'ayim /gII/6.tMassekhet Sukkah: text, translation, and commentary /rShulamit Valler ; 2009 --gII/7.tMassekhet Betsah: text, translation, and commentary /rTamara Or ; 2010 --gII/9.tMassekhet Ta'anit: text, translation, and commentary /rTal Ilan ; 2008 --gII/10.tMassekhet Mo'ed Qatan: text, translation, and commentary /rGail Labovitz ; 2021 --gIII/6/d-etMassekhet Gittin Chapters 4-5: text, translation, and commentary /rAnat Israeli, Tal Ilan ; 2024 --gIII/7/d.tMassekhet Qiddushin Chapter 4: text, translation, and commentary /rAnat Israeli in collaboration with Esther Fisher and Inbar Raveh ; 2021 --gV.tIntroduction to Seder Qodashim /redited by Tal Ilan, Monika Brockhaus and Tanja Hidde ; 2012 --gV/2.tMassekhet Menahot: text, translation, and commentary /rDvora Weisberg ; 2020 --gV/3.tMassekhet Hullin: text, translation, and commentary /rTal Ilan ; 2017 --gV/7.tMassekhet Keritot: text, translation, and commentary /rFederico Dal Bo ; 2013 --gV/9.tTractates Tamid, Middot and Qinnim: a feminist commentary /rDalia Marx ; 2013  aIn English with occasional texts in Hebrew or Aramaic00aTalmudxFeminist criticism.00aTalmudvCommentaries.00aMishnahxFeminist criticism.00aMishnahvCommentaries. 0aFeminismxReligious aspectsxJudaism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2006004724 0aWomen in rabbinical literature.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8514760006aTalmud0(CaQQLa)201-0017666xCritique féministe.0(CaQQLa)201-038062206aTalmud0(CaQQLa)201-0017666vCommentaires.0(CaQQLa)201-0378223 6aFemmes dans la littérature rabbinique.0(CaQQLa)201-01440211 aIlan, Tal,d1956-eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no930203501https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/en