ational Park and denaturalizes the project of conservation behind UNESCO's first "urban cultural landscape"; Ella Comberg seeks views of the street beyond what Doug Rickard's A New American Picture, and Google, ask us to see; Alexyss McClellan-Ufugusuku extends the recent COVID-19 outbreak at Marine Corps Air Station Futenma to legacies of dual colonization and militarization in Okinawa; Karamia Müller revisits her architectural education alongside the imperial conception of land that came with it; and Malcom Rio and Aaron Tobey examine the design of injustice in the case of the courthouse."--cprovided by distributor  aOther OA License10aArchitects.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500656510aArchitectural criticism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500658310aArchitecture.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500661110aArts--Study and teaching.10aCity planning.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8502628210aData mining.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh9700207310aEcology.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8504075210aImperialism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8506462810aPhotographic criticism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8600395510aRacism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8511026610aSustainable development.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh9200574310aTechnology and the arts.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8513318617aArchitects.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008131140http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81311417aArchitectural criticism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008131790http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81317917aArchitecture.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008133460http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81334617aArt and technology.2fast0(OCoLC)fst011452760http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81544117aArt Pedagogy.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0081533817aColonies.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009681260http://id.worldcat.org/fast/86845617aData mining.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008879460http://id.worldcat.org/fast/887946