aWatson, Amy,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n930707041 aWerner, Christian,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n911203831 aWesemann, Nina,econtributor.1 aWhite, Elliot,econtributor.1 aWolken, Nicholas,econtributor.2 aLibrary Stack,edistributor.40zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps://www.librarystack.org/corona-cookbook-the/yLibrary StackxProvider: Library StackxpurchasedxeLoaderURLxls4zTo create lists or check out books that are not open access, users must create a Library Stack account.xls3184642uhttps://www.librarystack.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/The_Corona_Cookbook_CVR-240x173.jpgzCover Image Preview  aeLoaderRecord xls4ffi4c7deb00-57e8-47dd-aed0-0956872c1031sdf9fd33e-7de0-49d1-b03f-b3757ac9018705468nam a2200733ui in0000030352620250403135145.0a||||go|||||||||||cr mn|---uuuuu181121s2004||||xx ||||go|||||||| u|eng|d  als5874  aNYHLSbengerdacNYHLSdCstdUtOrBLW00aHarun Farocki: Working on the Sight-Lines 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bAmsterdam University Press,c2004  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a"For more than thirty years Farocki has been a filmmaker, documentarist, film-essayist and installation artist. What preoccupies him above all is not so much an image of life, but the life of images, as they surround us in the newspapers, the cinema, history books, user manuals, posters, CCTV footage and advertising. His vast oeuvre of some sixty films includes three feature films (Zwischen den Kriegen/Between the Wars, Etwas wird sichtbar: Vietnam/In Your Eyes: Vietnam, Wie Man sieht/As You See), essay films (e.g. Images of the World-Inscription of War), critical media-pieces, experimental work, children's features for television, historical film essays (e.g. on Peter Lorre), `learning-films' in the tradition of Brecht (e.g. Workers Leaving the Factory) and installation pieces (e.g. Still Life). In this monograph, Elsaesser approaches Farocki's work from different critical perspectives, as well as reflecting on his extraordinary biography. The volume is complemented by interviews, a selection of writings by Farocki and an annotated filmography."--cprovided by distributor  aStandard Copyright10aArtists.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500827610aAutomation.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8501011610aCybernetics.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8503504610aFilm criticism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8508803910aMilitary art and science.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8508513210aMilitary-industrial complex.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8800156910aMotion pictures.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8508808410aPolitical art.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh201800299717aArtists.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008175590http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81755917aAutomation.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008227860http://id.worldcat.org/fast/82278617aCybernetics.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008857770http://id.worldcat.org/fast/88577717aFilm criticism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009242590http://id.worldcat.org/fast/92425917aFilmstrips.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010272850http://id.worldcat.org/fast/92431617aMilitary-industrial complex.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010216050http://id.worldcat.org/fast/102160517aPolitical art.2fast0(OCoLC)fst020036820http://id.worldcat.org/fast/200368217aMilitary art and science.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010208740http://id.worldcat.org/fast/1020874 7aDiscursive works.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026089 7aBook.2marcgt 7aEssay Collection.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0142403217aMicrofilms.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010198310http://id.worldcat.org/fast/101983117aMotion pictures.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010272850http://id.worldcat.org/fast/102728517aPhotographyxFilms.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01061