11 aWalker, Hamza,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n980660691 aWeisberg, Allison Freedman,econtributor.1 aWesley, Gee,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20221257081 aWong, Michelle Wun Ting,econtributor.2 aLibrary Stack,edistributor.2 aOther Means,eContributor.40zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps://www.librarystack.org/i-is-for-institute/yLibrary StackxProvider: Library StackxpurchasedxeLoaderURLxls4zTo create lists or check out books that are not open access, users must create a Library Stack account.xls5124642uhttps://www.librarystack.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/ICA-institute-copy-480x320.pngzCover Image Preview  aeLoaderRecord xls4ffi589b2e8f-040b-45ee-bfb3-09fa92d9bc2as8cb4a050-69f5-48a0-a48e-85f6d411f5b807675nam a2201057ui in0000030465420250403135215.0a||||go|||||||||||cr mn|---uuuuu231115s2016||||xx ||||go|||||||| u|eng|d  als148691  aNYHLSbengerdacNYHLSdCstdUtOrBLW00aacross & beyond: A transmediale Reader on Post-digital Practices, Concepts, and Institutions 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bSternberg Press,c2016 1a[Place of publication not identified] :btransmediale,c2016  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a"This collection of art and theory analyzes today's post-digital conditions for critical media practices-moving across and beyond the analog and the digital, the human and the nonhuman. The contributions also look across and beyond the field of media art, staking out new paths for understanding and working in the transversal territories between theory, technology, and art. The concept of the post-digital is a way to critically take account of, contextualize, and shift the coordinates of new technologies as part of contemporary culture. The post-digital condition is not merely a theoretical issue but also a situation that affects conceptual and practice-based work. The program of the transmediale festival in Berlin, celebrating its thirtieth year in 2017, has reflected these changes, and this book gathers new contributions from theorists and artists that have taken part in the festival program over its past five editions. Divided into the thematic sections Imaginaries, Interventions, and Ecologies, the book is not a document of the festival itself but a standalone volume that explores the ongoing themes of transmediale in a book format."--cprovided by distributor  aCC BY-SA10aAlgorithms.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500348710aArtificial intelligence.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500818010aAutomation.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8501011610aDigital media.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh9800660010aDrone aircraft.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8503962310aElectronic surveillance in art.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh200300004610aNatural language processing (Computer science)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8800242510aNew media art.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh200900503010aTechnology and the arts.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8513318610aUser interfaces (Computer systems)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8800167917aAlgorithms.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008050200http://id.worldcat.org/fast/80502017aArt and technology.2fast0(OCoLC)fst011452760http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81544117aArtificial intelligence.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008172470http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81724717aAutomation.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008227860http://id.worldcat.org/fast/82278617aDigital media.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008937160http://id.worldcat.org/fast/89371617aDrones.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0089834917aNatural Language Processing.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0103436517aNew media art.2fast0(OCoLC)fst017481910http://id.worldcat.org/fast/174819117aSurveillance