merican classics (Naxos (Sound recording label))0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no990252721 aBarber, Samuel,d1910-1981.tOrchestra music (Naxos (Sound recording label)) ;vv. 2.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no2002110397  aSUL/MUSIC/catalogedby/Flourish-WS/202410  aSUL/MUSIC/gift/kevkishi/20241106/Baxter  b36105234614068cMCD 74347n1lMusic PAGE-MU (MUS-PAGE-MU)  aC0bSTFffs48710078-7e7f-4475-ac53-4bfb0801e1ebi595c07bd-5ee4-42a7-980c-d305cd5cd9e808854nam a2201441ui in0000029994520250403135216.0a||||go|||||||||||cr mn|---uuuuu220518s2011||||xx ||||go|||||||| u|eng|d  als95158  aNYHLSbengerdacNYHLSdCstdUtOrBLW00aI Read Where I Am: Exploring New Information Cultures 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bGraphic Design Museum,c2011 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bInstitute of Network Cultures,c2011 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bValiz,c2011  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a"I Read Where I Am contains visionary texts about the future of reading and the status of the word. We read anytime and anywhere. We read of screens, we read out on the streets, we read in the office but less and less we read a book at home on the couch. We are, or are becoming, a different type of reader. How will we grapple with compressed narratives and the fluid bombardment of text? What are the dialectics between image and word? How will our information machines generate new reading cultures? Can reading become a live, mobile social experience? To answer all these (and other) questions, I Read Where I Am displays 82 diverse observations, inspirations and critical notes by journalists, designers, researchers, politicians, philosophers and many others."--cprovided by distributor  aCC BY-NC-SA10aArt and literature.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500796210aDigital media.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh9800660010aInformation commons.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh200600638017aArts and Literature.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0081540017aDigital media.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008937160http://id.worldcat.org/fast/89371617aInformation commons.2fast0(OCoLC)fst017652060http://id.worldcat.org/fast/1765206 7aDiscursive works.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026089 7aEssay Collection.2fast0(OCoLC)fst014240321 aAltena, Arie,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20090099691 aBlanken, Henk,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n970294171 aBlauvelt, Andrew,eauthor.1 aBlom, Erwin,eauthor.1 aBridle, James,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20180154701 aBruinsma, Max,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n880605811 aBurdick, Anne,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20120456081 aCampanelli, Vito,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20110178911 aCramer, Florian,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nb991389791 aDockray, Sean,eauthor.1 aDresscher, Paulien,eauthor.1 aEhmann, Sven,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nb20043145091 aEngelenburg, René van,eauthor.1 aFerro-Thomsen, Martin,eauthor.1 aGerritzen, Mieke,d1962-eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20020217801 aGomez, Jeff,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n931150431 aGonzales Crisp, Denise,eauthor.1 aGriekspoor, Alexander,eauthor.1 aGrievink, Hendrik-Jan,eauthor.1 aGroot, Ger,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n990357861 aHaak, Bregtje van der,eauthor.1 aHall, Gary,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no980525441 aHaltiwanger, John,eauthor.1 aHayles, N. Katherine,eauthor.1 aHorsten, Toon,eauthor.1 aJole, Francisco van,eauthor.1 aKampman, Minke,eeditor,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20120321461 aKaplanian-Bulle